# Reading the model as DBML

## Text notation for tables + relationships

```dbml
Table FactSales {
  sales_key      integer [primary key]
  customer_key   integer [not null]
  order_id       integer [note: 'degenerate dimension']
  quantity       integer
  line_total     decimal(12,2)
}
Ref: FactSales.customer_key > DimCustomer.customer_key
```

## How to read it

- **`Table { }`** — a table; each line = **column · type · tags**
- **`[primary key]`** = surrogate PK · **`[not null]`** = required FK · **`[note]`** = intent
- **`Ref: … > …`** = one **edge of the star** (FK → PK, many-to-one)

## Why DBML

- **Version-controlled & reviewable** — text, diffs like code
- **Single source** of the physical model · **renders an ERD** (dbdiagram.io)
